Body:
### Upstream Root Cause & Architectural Investigation

Investigated the link rendering behavior in `packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx` (`<markdown conceal={ctx.conceal()} ... />`).

#### 1. Source Ownership & Boundary
The Markdown inline token rendering logic (`case "link"`) lives entirely inside upstream dependency **`@opentui/core`** (specifically in its internal markdown token renderer), rather than inside OpenCode repository source:

- When `conceal: true` is active, `@opentui/core` unconditionally formats markdown links by appending `" (" + href + ")"` chunks:
  ```js
  case "link": {
    let $ = { url: _.href };
    if (this._conceal) {
      for (let Z of _.tokens)
        this.renderInlineTokenWithStyle(Z, J, "markup.link.label", $);
      J.push(this.createChunk(" (", "markup.link", $));
      J.push(this.createChunk(_.href, "markup.link.url", $));
      J.push(this.createChunk(")", "markup.link", $));
    }
  }
  ```
- OpenCode uses `@opentui/solid` / `@opentui/core`'s built-in `<markdown>` component directly and passes formatting options (such as `conceal`, `syntaxStyle`, `tableOptions`), but `@opentui/core` does not expose a public token-render hook or markdown AST visitor to customize inline link chunk emission from consumer code.

#### 2. Conclusion & Recommended Upstream Resolution
- **Outcome**: `UPSTREAM_DEPENDENCY` / No local OpenCode code patch.
- **Recommended Upstream Fix (in `@opentui/core`)**: Make link formatting in `@opentui/core` capability-aware (e.g. check terminal OSC 8 hyperlink support / `setHyperlinksCapability` when `conceal: true`). In terminals supporting OSC 8, emit only the label tokens styled with `{ url: href }` and omit the trailing `" (" + href + ")"` chunks; keep the expanded fallback format for terminals lacking OSC 8 support.
